;; ABSTRACTION-VERDICT-1 A4: a false post (f 4 = -1). Before CALL-CONGRUENCE-1
;; it fell back as abstraction:app:f, the stated cost. With the congruence fact
;; the counterexample is a real function, so f is refuted again.
(def-shell f [n: int] -> int (pre (>= n 0)) (post (>= result 0)) (if (< n 2) n (- (f (- n 1)) (f (- n 2)))))
